SOAPBOX: This was another WQ6X QRP operation running remote from ANZA this time.
SOAPBOX: The band condx. were a AMAZingly AWEsome - my only regret was no access
SOAPBOX: to the radio for the 1st 5-hours and then the off time on Saturday due
SOAPBOX: to a CQP presentation for the Amateur Radio Club of Alameda (ARCA).
SOAPBOX: Having access to Stacked Yagi's on 40 - 10 meters and an 80-meter 4-square
SOAPBOX: vertical array made WQ6X's QRP signal sound like 200+ watts.
SOAPBOX: My biggest beef were stations who called CQ EXACTLY on my oddly chosen run
SOAPBOX: frequency (Ex: 28131.31 or 21162.62), so I know it was no accident.
SOAPBOX: Wassup with RTTY operation EXACTLY on 14.100 QRM'ing the NCDXF beacon -
SOAPBOX: that is pretty LAME (and LiDDiSH) if you ask me.
SOAPBOX: SOAPBOX: A few internet dropouts made me disappear alluva sudden.
SOAPBOX: So if I disappeared it wasn't personal - it was IP-based.
SOAPBOX: Look for a write-up on this GiG at: http://WQ6X.Blogspot.com
